Z||000004||StuGood||12-19-2000||06:42 PM||||Cheer up... it doesn't <B>always</B> happen to everyone... and it's happened to almost everybody at <B>least</B> once  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  There're a few Fieros I could've had, but lost out on.  In fact, you could say I've missed out on a few cars (including a Fiero convertible  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ), and even a screen door one time (I'll be kind, and spare you the long story on <B>that</B> one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> )!<P>Usually helps to have the cash on hand - money really looks good to someone who needs it (been there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )!<P>In my case, I normally do business at my local bank.  Reasons:  1)Lots of witnesses (and cameras), 2) People at the bank can notarize the title right then and there,  3) I can withdraw the money at the bank, instead of carrying that kind of cash around in my pocket, 4) Gets you and the seller to a "neutral" location; nobody shows up and outbids you on the spot.<P>Once the seller agrees to the price, I immediately suggest we go over to the bank, so he/she can get their money right away.  They usually seem to appreciate it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !<P>Meantime, as I always say, anything worth having is worth waiting for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !         ||||reg||6
Z||000005||DavidHenshaw||12-19-2000||08:35 PM||||IMHO the fact that there aren't 10 million Fieros around like the Firebirds and Mustangs is a big plus. Please don't flame about the two I mentioned, they are nice cars I just like Fieros better. Its does seem however like the particular one you want is always 1200 miles away. <P>Its common to see 4 cyls a little beat up selling for $400 to $600 but the nicer 6 cyl cars with decent bodies are listed for $2000 and up.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
